# Technical Taxonomy

Two classifications go into every report. Both must appear in the final output with the full description of the chosen level/style included verbatim, so the reader has context without needing to look up what "Level 3" or "hybrid" means.

---

## 3b. AI Maturity Level

Assess where the company currently sits on the AI maturity scale. This is a classification, not a value ranking — being at Level 4 instead of Level 3 is not inherently better. What matters is whether the current level matches the workflow potential, and how large the gap is between where the company is and where it could credibly reach.

| Level | Label | Description |
|-------|-------|-------------|
| 1 | None | No AI in the product. If the workflow type supports AI integration, this represents high effort but also high upside. |
| 2 | Integration | AI models incorporated off-the-shelf via API, with genuine feature-market fit — not cosmetic, but meaningfully improving UX and willingness to pay. Most AI-enabled software sits here. Replicable by competitors without a proprietary edge. |
| 3 | Orchestration | Significant engineering around the edges of base models to improve performance for customers: data/context structuring, prompt engineering, model routing, output optimisation, evals. The company has processes to extract maximum value from available models. A legitimate and often sufficient competitive position. |
| 4 | Fine-tuning | Moving from engineering around models to enhancing the models themselves: supervised fine-tuning on proprietary datasets, distillation, quantisation, reinforcement learning. Produces faster, cheaper, purpose-built models. Requires data scientists and ML engineers — validate against team composition. |
| 5 | Foundation | Pre-training proprietary foundational models. Extremely rare outside of dedicated AI labs. Almost never relevant for B2B vertical software targets. |

**The gap that matters.** Identify the current level, the realistic ceiling given the workflow nature and data assets, and whether the distance between them represents untapped value or an unrealistic ambition.

**How to present this in the report.** State the chosen level (e.g., "Level 2 — Integration"), quote the level's description verbatim from the table above, then add a short paragraph on: (a) what evidence in the sources supports the classification, (b) the realistic ceiling, (c) the gap.

